; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Traffic Light
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     animation, WAIT, procedures with inputs, timing, colors
; SUMMARY:  Runs a traffic light through red, green and yellow, with a walking sign that changes too.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Draws a traffic light on a pole. One lamp at a time is lit
;   brightly while the others are dim. The light stays red for a
;   while, then green, then a short yellow, and starts again. A sign
;   beside it says WALK or WAIT.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Press Stop to end. Change the numbers given
;   to WAIT in CYCLE to make each color last longer.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * WAIT n pauses for n sixtieths of a second
;   * one LAMP procedure used for all three lamps
;   * drawing a lamp bright or dim with a true/false input
;   * a cycle that repeats forever
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add a flashing yellow at night (on, off, on, off).
;   * Make the green last twice as long as the red.
;   * Draw a second light that shows the opposite colors.
; ============================================================

; LAMP draws one round lamp at height :y. If :on is "true it uses the
; bright color, otherwise the dim one.
to lamp :y :bright :dim :on
  ifelse :on [setpencolor :bright] [setpencolor :dim]
  setpensize 70
  dot list 0 :y
end

; HOUSING draws the black box and the pole.
to housing
  setpencolor [40 40 40]
  setpensize 20
  penup setxy 0 -270 setheading 0 pendown
  forward 160
  penup setxy -55 -110 pendown
  filled [30 30 30] [repeat 2 [forward 280 right 90 forward 110 right 90]]
end

; SIGN writes WALK or WAIT next to the light.
to sign :text :color
  setpencolor :color
  setlabelheight 40
  penup setxy 100 0 pendown
  label :text
end

; SHOW.LIGHT redraws everything with one lamp lit.
to show.light :which
  clean
  housing
  lamp 100 [255 40 40] [80 20 20] :which = "red
  lamp 30 [255 210 40] [80 70 20] :which = "yellow
  lamp -40 [40 220 80] [20 70 30] :which = "green
  ifelse :which = "red [sign "WALK [40 180 80]] [sign "WAIT [220 60 60]]
end

; CYCLE goes once through the colors. WAIT 60 is one second.
to cycle
  show.light "red
  wait 180
  show.light "green
  wait 180
  show.light "yellow
  wait 60
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [200 225 240]
forever [cycle]
